<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n65604" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέθεξις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>, ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετέχω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>participation</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐσίας μετὰ χρόνου</span>
			<i>participation</i> of being in time, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Prm.</u>
				151e
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρόνου</span> in time, ib.<i><span class="en">
				141d
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ μ. τῶν ἀρχῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1278a23
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in Platonic
			philosophy, <i>participation</i> in the ideas, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ μ. τοῖς ἄλλοις . . τῶν εἰδῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Prm.</u>
					132d
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Metaph.</u>
				987b10
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταὐτοῦ</span>
			<i>in</i> the same, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Sph.</u>
				256b
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> in Logic,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ μέθεξιν</span> as <i>being
				contained</i> or <i>comprehended</i>, as genus or difference
			in species, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Top.</u>
				132b35
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
